                "retweet_count": 17,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "As a veteran myself, I want to take a moment to recognize PTSD Awareness Month. Many of our brave servicemen and women face the invisible wounds of war long after their service ends. It's vital that we raise awareness about PTSD, break the stigma surrounding mental health, and ensure that our veterans receive the support they need. \n\nIf you or someone you know is struggling, remember that help is available. Visit https://t.co/ItxZV11CWm for resources or call 988 and push 1 for the crisis hotline. \n\nLet\u2019s work together to foster a culture of understanding and compassion, ensuring that no one has to face these challenges alone. Your fight is our fight, and you are never forgotten.",
                "text_lang": "en",
                "text_tagged_users": null,
                "text_tagged_users_ids": null,
                "text_tags": null,
                "timestamp": 1748871251,
